{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UFD6Ai4emkZjrveKx3fi19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `picoquic/picoquictest_dualq.h` (with bodies in\n2\t//! `picoquictest/dualq_aqm.c`).\n3\t//!\n4\t//! DualQ-Coupled AQM used by the test suite (RFC 9332 timestamp\n5\t//! variant).  Sits behind a [`TestSimLink`]'s `aqm_state` slot and\n6\t//! classifies arriving packets into an L4S queue ([`Dualq::lq`]) or\n7\t//! a Classic queue ([`Dualq::cq`]); marks/drops on dequeue using the\n8\t//! PI2 controller; and feeds admitted packets back into the link's\n9\t//! transit queue.\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every function body is\n12\t//! `todo!()`.  Bodies and the empty test module land in later\n13\t//! phases.\n14\t//!\n15\t//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n16\t//!\n17\t//! * The C vtable struct `picoquictest_aqm_t` is already a Rust\n18\t//!   trait ([`TestAqm`](crate::tests::util::TestAqm)) in\n19\t//!   [`crate::utils`].  The C \"embed `super` and cast pointer\"\n20\t//!   inheritance pattern collapses to `impl TestAqm for Dualq`; the\n21\t//!   C `super` field is dropped.\n22\t//! * The C dualq pair of `queue_first` / `queue_last` raw\n23\t//!   `*mut TestSimPacket` heads (the intrusive-linked-list shape\n24\t//!   used by the parent sim-link) is replaced by an owning\n25\t//!   `VecDeque<TestSimPacket>` per queue.  Submit pushes;\n26\t//!   dequeue pops.  No raw pointers, no `unsafe`.\n27\t//! * The C `dualq_dequeue_one`'s `int* should_drop` out-parameter\n28\t//!   folds into a tuple return — `Option<(Box<...>, bool)>`\n29\t//!   represents \"no packet ready\" / \"(packet, drop?)\".\n30\t//! * The C `dualq_release` self-frees with `free(self)` and clears\n31\t//!   `link->aqm_state`.  In Rust the trait method takes\n32\t//!   `&mut self`; the actual deallocation rides on the\n33\t//!   `Option<Box<dyn TestAqm>>` slot in the link being reset to\n34\t//!   `None` by the caller after `release` drains the queues —\n35\t//!   `release` itself only handles the queue drain.\n36\t\n37\tuse crate::Error;\n38\tuse crate::Instant;\n39\tuse crate::tests::util::{TestAqm, TestSimLink, TestSimPacket};\n40\t\n41\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n42\t// Tunables.\n43\t\n44\t/// Simulation link-rate ceiling: 125,000,000 bytes/sec ≈ 1 Gbps.\n45\t/// C: `#define DUALQ_MAX_LINK_RATE 125000000`.\n46\tpub const DUALQ_MAX_LINK_RATE: u64 = 125_000_000;\n47\t\n48\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n49\t// Per-queue state.\n50\t\n51\t/// One classified queue (L4S or Classic) inside a [`Dualq`].\n52\t/// C: `dualq_queue_t`.\n53\t///\n54\t/// Storage shape:\n55\t///\n56\t/// * The C `queue_first` / `queue_last` pair (intrusive linked\n57\t///   list, same pattern as [`crate::tests::util::TestSimLink`])\n58\t///   is replaced by an owning `VecDeque<TestSimPacket>`.  Submit\n59\t///   pushes to the back; dequeue pops from the front and hands\n60\t///   ownership to the caller via [`Dualq::dequeue_one`].\n61\t/// * `count` mirrors the C `int`, kept as `i32` for ABI parity with\n62\t///   the dualq tests that inspect it directly.\n63\t#[derive(Default)]\n64\tpub struct DualqQueue {\n65\t    pub queue_bytes: u64,\n66\t    /// Running sum of drop probability — when it crosses 1.0 the\n67\t    /// `dualq_recur` helper \"fires\" and the head packet is\n68\t    /// dropped/marked.  C: `double sum_p`.\n69\t    pub sum_p: f64,\n70\t    /// Packets in the queue.  Replaces the C `queue_first` /\n71\t    /// `queue_last` head/tail pair.  `count` is `packets.len()`\n72\t    /// (the C field is gone).\n73\t    pub packets: std::collections::VecDeque<TestSimPacket>,\n74\t}\n75\t\n76\timpl DualqQueue {\n77\t    /// Append `packet` to the tail of this queue.\n78\t    /// C: `dualq_enqueue_queue(dualq_queue_t* xq,\n79\t    /// picoquictest_sim_packet_t* packet)`.\n80\t    pub fn enqueue(&mut self, _packet: TestSimPacket) {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17072f18-9969-498e-bec6-45838e44ca80","uuid":"8c48b5b4-93b8-4237-b107-1fdbf644ef89","timestamp":"2026-05-05T03:00:22.015Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/dualq.rs","content":"//! Translation of `picoquic/picoquictest_dualq.h` (with bodies in\n//! `picoquictest/dualq_aqm.c`).\n//!\n//! DualQ-Coupled AQM used by the test suite (RFC 9332 timestamp\n//! variant).  Sits behind a [`TestSimLink`]'s `aqm_state` slot and\n//! classifies arriving packets into an L4S queue ([`Dualq::lq`]) or\n//! a Classic queue ([`Dualq::cq`]); marks/drops on dequeue using the\n//! PI2 controller; and feeds admitted packets back into the link's\n//! transit queue.\n//!\n//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every function body is\n//! `todo!()`.  Bodies and the empty test module land in later\n//! phases.\n//!\n//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n//!\n//! * The C vtable struct `picoquictest_aqm_t` is already a Rust\n//!   trait ([`TestAqm`](crate::tests::util::TestAqm)) in\n//!   [`crate::utils`].  The C \"embed `super` and cast pointer\"\n//!   inheritance pattern collapses to `impl TestAqm for Dualq`; the\n//!   C `super` field is dropped.\n//! * The C dualq pair of `queue_first` / `queue_last` raw\n//!   `*mut TestSimPacket` heads (the intrusive-linked-list shape\n//!   used by the parent sim-link) is replaced by an owning\n//!   `VecDeque<TestSimPacket>` per queue.  Submit pushes;\n//!   dequeue pops.  No raw pointers, no `unsafe`.\n//! * The C `dualq_dequeue_one`'s `int* should_drop` out-parameter\n//!   folds into a tuple return — `Option<(Box<...>, bool)>`\n//!   represents \"no packet ready\" / \"(packet, drop?)\".\n//! * The C `dualq_release` self-frees with `free(self)` and clears\n//!   `link->aqm_state`.  In Rust the trait method takes\n//!   `&mut self`; the actual deallocation rides on the\n//!   `Option<Box<dyn TestAqm>>` s