{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user presented a **Phase 3A batch test-body translation task** for the `c2rust` branch of picoquic. The task is to translate C test bodies from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies in `rs/fq/src/tests/`. The mandate is TDD: tests need to **compile** (even if they panic at `todo!()` stubs), express the test intent faithfully, and NOT leave entire bodies as `todo!()`. Five source files covering 47 tests total are in scope:\n   - `datagram_tests` (11 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/datagram.rs`\n   - `delay_tolerant_test` (4 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/delay_tolerant.rs`\n   - `dualq_aqm_test` (1 test) → `rs/fq/src/tests/dualq_aqm.rs`\n   - `ech_test` (6 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/ech.rs`\n   - `edge_cases` (25 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/edge_cases.rs`\n\n   The final gate is: `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py [all 5 sources]`, `cargo fmt`, `cargo test --no-run`, `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Rust/C translation**: C `picoquic_xxx(cnx, …)` → Rust methods; C structs → Rust structs with Rust naming conventions\n   - **`todo!()` stub pattern**: any API not yet implemented gets a `todo!()` stub in `lib.rs` or `internal.rs` with a `/// C: picoquic_xxx` doc-comment\n   - **`TestTlsApiCtx`**: the central test infrastructure struct holding client/server `Quic` contexts, two sim links, and connection handles\n   - **`TestSimLink` / `TestAqm` / `Dualq`**: network simulator and DualQ AQM for test infrastructure\n   - **`tls_api_init_ctx_ex`**: creates the test context (server+client Quic, connections, sim links)\n   - **`tls_api_one_scenario_body`** / `tls_api_connection_loop` / `tls_api_one_sim_round`: simulation loop helpers (all `todo!()`)\n   - **E