{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user presented a **Phase 3A batch test-body translation task** for the `c2rust` branch of picoquic. The mandate was TDD: translate C test bodies from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies in `rs/fq/src/tests/`, ensuring they compile (even if they panic at `todo!()` stubs), express the test intent faithfully, and do NOT leave entire bodies as `todo!()`. Five source files covering 47 tests were in scope. The final gate: `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py [all 5 sources]`, `cargo fmt`, `cargo test --no-run`, `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Rust/C translation**: C `picoquic_xxx(cnx, …)` → Rust methods on `Connection`/`Quic`\n   - **`todo!()` stub pattern**: any API not yet implemented gets `todo!()` bodies; tests compile and express intent even if they panic at runtime\n   - **`TestTlsApiCtx`**: central test infrastructure struct with `qclient`, `qserver`, two sim links, connection handles\n   - **`DatagramSendRecvCtx`**: per-test state for datagram callbacks; mirrors `test_datagram_send_recv_ctx_t`\n   - **`DtnTestSpec`**: configuration struct for delay-tolerant networking scenarios\n   - **`EchE2eSpec`**: parameters for ECH end-to-end scenarios\n   - **`ResetTestKind` / `ResetStreamAtSpec`**: enums for parameterized reset-stream tests\n   - **Clippy `-D warnings` gate**: all dead-code warnings, unused-import warnings must be resolved\n   - **`phase3_check.py`**: verification script that checks each source's tests are not pure `todo!()` stubs\n   - **DualQ AQM**: 5 sub-tests chained in the single `dualq_aqm` test entry\n   - **ECH (Encrypted Client Hello)**: `ech_create_config_from_public_key/private_key`, `ech_save_config`, `ech_read